meta {
  name: Document Upload
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/apis/{{site}}/api/copilot/document
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "patient_uuid": "{{patientUuid}}",
    "doc_type": "lab_pdf",
    "filename": "cbc-panel.pdf",
    "file_content_b64": "JVBERi0xLjcgdGlueSBicnVubyBwbGFjZWhvbGRlciBieXRlcwo="
  }
}

docs {
  # Document Upload

  UC6 — `POST /api/copilot/document`, one of this module's two sanctioned
  writes (founder-approved 2026-07-13): attaches the uploaded document to
  `patient_uuid` (dedupe-by-hash) and runs VLM extraction against the
  committed `lab_pdf`/`intake_form` JSON Schemas, persisting extracted
  facts as observations provenance-linked back to this document. Requires
  the `user/document.write` scope and the `patients`/`med` ACL. Both steps
  execute as the delegated physician — never a service account.

  ## Content mode (this request)

  `file_content_b64` above is a TINY placeholder base64 payload
  (`%PDF-1.7 tiny bruno placeholder bytes`) standing in for real PDF/PNG/
  JPEG bytes — swap it for `base64 < your-file.pdf | tr -d '\n'` when
  exercising this against a live document. This is the browser-reachable
  upload shape: a static page cannot supply a server-side path, so it
  sends raw bytes instead. `filename`'s extension must be one of
  pdf/png/jpg/jpeg.

  Set `"doc_type": "intake_form"` to exercise the other extraction schema
  (chief concern, current medications, allergies, family history,
  demographics — all per-field cited, absent-not-defaulted per D1).

  ## Path mode (alternative, not browser-reachable)

  A server-side-path caller (CLI/tooling with filesystem access to the
  OpenEMR host) may instead send `"file_path": "/tmp/uploads/cbc-panel.pdf"`
  + `"file_size_bytes": 48213` in place of `filename`/`file_content_b64`.
  Exactly one mode is accepted — both or neither is refused as
  ambiguous/incomplete (400).

  A successful response's `document_id` feeds the Source Resolve request's
  `lab_pdf:<document_id>#<field_path>` / `intake_form:<document_id>#<field_path>`
  token — the click-to-source loop this collection demonstrates end to end.
}
